WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:06.144
Here at the sanctuary we have our own motto that we believe in. It’s

00:00:06.656 --> 00:00:08.960
“Saving one animal may not change the world,

00:00:09.472 --> 00:00:12.032
but surely for that one animal the world will change forever.”

00:00:12.544 --> 00:00:18.000
And we fully believe that because we see it every day.

00:00:18.944 --> 00:00:25.088
My name is Pat Craig. I’m the executive director and founder of the Wild Animal Sanctuary located in Keenesburg, Colorado.

00:00:27.344 --> 00:00:31.488
The sanctuary was started 36 years ago. I visited a zoo one time and I was really surprised to see all these

00:00:31.744 --> 00:00:34.560
lions and tigers in the back kept in tiny little cages and

00:00:34.816 --> 00:00:37.632
I found out they were surplus and that they actually euthanize those animals.

00:00:38.912 --> 00:00:43.008
So I opened the first sanctuary in the country for large carnivores.

00:00:44.032 --> 00:00:50.176
So in the beginning I started on the family farm right outside of Boulder, Colorado that at the time, you know I dropped out of school

00:00:50.432 --> 00:00:52.480
and started working full-time to support the animals and

00:00:52.992 --> 00:00:55.040
build more space and go get more animals.

00:00:55.296 --> 00:00:59.392
We started to get phone calls from law enforcement agencies who were finding them in apartments and basements.

00:01:04.768 --> 00:01:07.400
About 85 percent of all the animals here were legal confiscations

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.120
from people who either abused them or had them illegally.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:15.008
The rest either come from zoos, circuses or other places like that that have them.

00:01:16.288 --> 00:01:20.000
We have over 420 rescued carnivores living here -

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:24.736
everything from wolves, tigers, bears,

00:01:25.248 --> 00:01:30.368
lions, leopards, mountain lions, you name it I mean there's a lot of mouths to feed.

00:01:30.624 --> 00:01:33.272
We feed over 38,000 pounds of food a week.

00:01:36.256 --> 00:01:39.072
These animals are absolutely like my kids just because

00:01:39.328 --> 00:01:42.000
This is my life turned into a seven-day-a-week,

00:01:42.652 --> 00:01:45.472
365-day-a-year job that I’ve been doing for 36 years and

00:01:45.984 --> 00:01:50.080
yeah there is no time to go anywhere for vacations or anything else, it's all for the animals.

00:01:51.616 --> 00:01:55.968
Wasn't something I expected to do and I had no idea how monumental it was going to get but

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:58.528
it's been worth every bit of the time so,

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:01.576
I wouldn't have changed it all.

